From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:24:27 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(compression): decision ledger kept outside the
 summary

Opt-in compression.decision_ledger_chars. A summary is rewritten by a model at every compaction, so a terse approval loses the question it answered, a dispatched build loses its id, and a peer's claim can drift into 'the user approved'. With the key set, each compaction scans the rows it removes by rule, without a model call: the user's own words (0068 classifier: typed messages with the assistant question each answered, hub page answers with the page title, mid-turn steers, clarify answers), questions left for the user, delegate_task dispatches with their ids settled by the matching async result, and tags, releases and workflow runs from terminal commands. The ledger rides at the end of the handoff as a '## Decision Ledger' block, verbatim; the summarizer never sees or rewrites it. Only user-authored rows become USER entries: a peer, subagent or tool that claims an approval never does. A ledger tool (offered only while the key is set) lists, adds, closes and searches entries; its entries are labeled AGENT. Past the cap the oldest settled entries move to $HERMES_HOME/decision-ledger/<session>.md. 0 = off; nothing changes then.
